\code{edge.length.symmetry.tolerance} is the nonnegative tolerance for matching
lengths on the two orientations of an undirected edge. Neighbor lists and
lengths are parallel; zero lengths are allowed. The inherited \code{weight.list}
name in \code{\link[=lcor]{lcor()}} and \code{\link[=lslope]{lslope()}} also supplies edge lengths, not vertex masses
